SWEET AMP PCM DETECT (patch 0389, plan A10e), on top of 0388: boot-arg sweetaoc=11 = sweetaoc=10 (HAL amp words, power-up, meters) with a
new diagnostic window that settles whether PCM reaches the amps. The DAC is fed from ASPRX1 (0x08, DSP out of the speaker path, as pattern
5) and the CSPL firmware's VMON / IMON inputs DSP1_RX3_SRC 0x4C48 / DSP1_RX4_SRC 0x4C4C (reset 0x18 / 0x19, AMP cs35l41-tables.c:81-82; Linux
v6.18 cs35l41.h:95-96, :631-645) are pointed at ASPRX1, so CSPL_TEMPERATURE / SPK_OUTPUT_POWER / BDLOG_* meter the received PCM. Control V:
RX3 / RX4 := VPMON 0x28 (never zero); S: ASPRX1, silence; pattern 6 = 2 beeps, AOC as is (ASP_ON); then "AoC Speaker Mixer ASP Mode"
:= ASP_BYPASS 2 (CMD_AUDIO_OUTPUT_SET_PARAMETER 209 block 16 component 2 key 0, aoc_set_asp_mode aoc_alsa_hw.c:1039-1065, texts
aoc_alsa_ctl.c:2434-2436; read back with GET_PARAMETER 211) and pattern 7 = 3 beeps; pattern 8 = 4 beeps with RX3 / RX4 back on VMON / IMON
(the speaker); then ASP mode := ASP_ON 1 (the value every earlier run read), DAC source DSP, snapshot end, the 0384 power-down. Meter lines
"d3" (RX3, RX4, DAC src, VPBR_STATUS, VBBR_STATUS, VOL_STATUS_TO_DSP, NGATE1_SRC; read only) + CSPL meters at V, S, D1/D0, E1/E0, F1/F0
(1 = in the first beep, 0 = in the gap after it). Levels <= 10 unchanged. USER DECISION 2026-11-18: speed first, no mutants.

